00:00:53.804 --> 00:00:56.604 position:63%
As a romantic in terms of mathematics,

00:00:56.904 --> 00:00:58.754 position:63%
what you describe would be horrible.

00:00:59.636 --> 00:01:02.101 position:63%
I would want a human being involved in the

00:01:02.101 --> 00:01:04.681 position:63%
proof and I'd like to believe that the proof

00:01:04.681 --> 00:01:07.376 position:63%
is beautiful and if it isn't beautiful I don't

00:01:07.376 --> 00:01:10.186 position:63%
think the search for a beautiful conceptual proof

00:01:12.404 --> 00:01:13.554 position:63%
Would be any less important.

00:01:13.554 --> 00:01:15.079 position:63%
Well, I personally would get like

00:01:15.079 --> 00:01:16.604 position:63%
a very sick enjoyment out of that.

00:01:17.054 --> 00:01:20.021 position:63%
I'm a logician whose research tends to be in

00:01:20.021 --> 00:01:22.593 position:63%
metamathematics, so I find the idea of

00:01:22.593 --> 00:01:25.626 position:63%
inscrutable proofs like kind of a fascinating

00:01:25.626 --> 00:01:26.154 position:63%
concept.

00:01:26.204 --> 00:01:27.304 position:63%
Is it even a danger?

00:01:27.404 --> 00:01:28.554 position:63%
Like maybe it just wouldn't matter.

00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:29.882 position:63%
Like, you know, in other words,

00:01:29.882 --> 00:01:31.534 position:63%
I've always said this that like, you know,

00:01:31.534 --> 00:01:33.454 position:63%
if there's a lean proof of the Riemann hypothesis

00:01:33.454 --> 00:01:35.220 position:63%
that's like, you know, 20 billion tokens long

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:36.104 position:63%
and nobody can read it,

00:01:36.204 --> 00:01:37.623 position:63%
that's not a proof of the Riemann hypothesis

00:01:37.623 --> 00:01:38.854 position:63%
and I just don't care that that exists.

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:39.670 position:63%
Don't you see?

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:41.449 position:63%
So I wouldn't consider that dangerous.

00:01:41.449 --> 00:01:43.137 position:63%
I would just be like, okay, too bad,

00:01:43.137 --> 00:01:45.236 position:63%
hopefully someday we'll figure out the proof.

00:01:45.236 --> 00:01:47.199 position:63%
That would present an opportunity for some

00:01:47.199 --> 00:01:49.070 position:63%
really interesting mathematics to happen,

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:50.370 position:63%
but it might happen and it might not.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:53.420 position:63%
I mean, you are right that if that existed,

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.320 position:63%
people would be like, wow,

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:56.670 position:63%
let's try to make something.

00:01:57.236 --> 00:01:59.522 position:63%
out of this so that we can understand like why

00:01:59.522 --> 00:02:01.809 position:63%
the Riemann hypothesis is true but that effort

00:02:01.809 --> 00:02:04.048 position:63%
might fail and then we would sort of you know

00:02:04.048 --> 00:02:06.238 position:63%
we would sort of shift what we thought of as

00:02:06.238 --> 00:02:08.573 position:63%
like what the big problem was the problem would

00:02:08.573 --> 00:02:10.812 position:63%
be the sort of like either to understand like

00:02:10.812 --> 00:02:13.147 position:63%
what was going on in this like 20 billion token

00:02:13.147 --> 00:02:15.386 position:63%
stream or to just figure it out some other way

00:02:20.786 --> 00:02:21.836 position:63%
This is a great question.

00:02:23.316 --> 00:02:25.977 position:63%
First good news. We have a curated

00:02:25.977 --> 00:02:28.716 position:63%
statement of the Riemann hypothesis.

00:02:29.066 --> 00:02:31.527 position:63%
So the first thing we would do is run the

00:02:31.527 --> 00:02:34.457 position:63%
comparator and check if the proof checks there is

00:02:34.457 --> 00:02:37.211 position:63%
no exploits. Suppose the comparator says, yes,

00:02:37.211 --> 00:02:39.789 position:63%
this is a proof for the Riemann hypothesis,

00:02:39.789 --> 00:02:41.372 position:63%
and I checked it with two,

00:02:41.372 --> 00:02:43.716 position:63%
three different kernels. They all agree.

00:02:44.816 --> 00:02:46.846 position:63%
This is amazing. I mean, even if

00:02:46.846 --> 00:02:48.816 position:63%
nobody can understand initially.

00:02:49.908 --> 00:02:52.202 position:63%
Like I said, a proof is not static.

00:02:52.202 --> 00:02:55.198 position:63%
People would search breaking into it into PCs.

00:02:55.198 --> 00:02:58.002 position:63%
People would hear writes isolate fragments,

00:02:58.002 --> 00:03:00.806 position:63%
people would invest a lot of time trying to

00:03:00.806 --> 00:03:03.611 position:63%
understand these objects. If they have high

00:03:03.611 --> 00:03:06.033 position:63%
confidence that the proof is correct,

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:08.965 position:63%
they will spend time trying to understand it.

00:03:08.965 --> 00:03:11.897 position:63%
So we I I think would be a great day for math

00:03:11.897 --> 00:03:13.107 position:63%
if it just happens.

00:03:13.257 --> 00:03:15.034 position:63%
How plausible is it that if

00:03:15.034 --> 00:03:16.808 position:63%
we just keep traininging Yeah.

00:03:16.808 --> 00:03:18.624 position:63%
out AIs that get better and better

00:03:18.624 --> 00:03:20.428 position:63%
at solving problems in lean,

00:03:20.678 --> 00:03:21.884 position:63%
that they will continue to solve

00:03:21.884 --> 00:03:23.128 position:63%
more and more impressive problems,

00:03:23.227 --> 00:03:25.643 position:63%
and then we will in retrospect be surprised at

00:03:25.643 --> 00:03:28.212 position:63%
how little insight we got from some lean solution

00:03:28.212 --> 00:03:30.628 position:63%
to proving the Riemann hypothesis or something?

00:03:30.727 --> 00:03:32.164 position:63%
Or do you think it is a necessary

00:03:32.164 --> 00:03:33.558 position:63%
condition of solving the Riemann

00:03:33.558 --> 00:03:35.628 position:63%
hypothesis that the constructions which are made,

00:03:35.827 --> 00:03:37.477 position:63%
the definitions which are created,

00:03:37.528 --> 00:03:39.178 position:63%
even in the lean program,

00:03:39.428 --> 00:03:41.839 position:63%
have to advance our understanding of mathematics?

00:03:41.839 --> 00:03:43.528 position:63%
Or do you think it could just be...

00:03:43.528 --> 00:03:45.298 position:63%
The assembly could go to Google to Google.

00:03:45.348 --> 00:03:46.498 position:63%
Yeah, we don't know.

00:03:46.648 --> 00:03:48.177 position:63%
I mean, some problems have been

00:03:48.177 --> 00:03:49.993 position:63%
basically solved by pure brute force.

00:03:49.993 --> 00:03:52.048 position:63%
The four color theorem is a famous example.

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:54.632 position:63%
We have still not found a conceptually

00:03:54.632 --> 00:03:56.198 position:63%
elegant proof of this theorem.

00:03:56.298 --> 00:03:59.398 position:63%
It basically, and maybe we never will.

00:03:59.448 --> 00:04:01.616 position:63%
I mean, some problems may only be solvable

00:04:01.616 --> 00:04:03.481 position:63%
by just splitting into some enormous

00:04:03.481 --> 00:04:05.398 position:63%
number of cases and doing brute force.

00:04:06.388 --> 00:04:09.138 position:63%
an inside of computer analysis on each case.

00:04:09.388 --> 00:04:11.926 position:63%
I mean part of the reason that we we prize

00:04:11.926 --> 00:04:14.878 position:63%
problems like a hypothesis that we're pretty sure

00:04:14.878 --> 00:04:17.771 position:63%
that that something amazing has to a new type of

00:04:17.771 --> 00:04:20.723 position:63%
mathematics has to be created or a new connection

00:04:20.723 --> 00:04:23.320 position:63%
between two previously unconnected areas of

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:26.213 position:63%
mathematics has to be discovered to to make this

00:04:26.213 --> 00:04:29.106 position:63%
work we we don't even know what the shape of the

00:04:29.106 --> 00:04:29.638 position:63%
solution.

00:04:30.292 --> 00:04:30.941 position:63%
Yes, but...

00:04:32.084 --> 00:04:34.108 position:63%
It doesn't feel like a problem that will be

00:04:34.108 --> 00:04:36.224 position:63%
solved just by exhaustively checking cases or

00:04:36.224 --> 00:04:36.724 position:63%
something.

00:04:37.034 --> 00:04:38.384 position:63%
I mean, it could be false actually.

00:04:38.484 --> 00:04:40.584 position:63%
So we could actually,

00:04:40.684 --> 00:04:42.981 position:63%
okay, there is an unlikely scenario that

00:04:42.981 --> 00:04:45.278 position:63%
the hypothesis is false and that you can

00:04:45.278 --> 00:04:47.800 position:63%
just compute, oh, here's a zero off the line

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:50.434 position:63%
and a massive computer calculation verifies it.

00:04:50.634 --> 00:04:51.834 position:63%
That would be very disappointing.

00:04:51.984 --> 00:04:54.942 position:63%
I do feel that fully autonomous one-shot

00:04:54.942 --> 00:04:57.684 position:63%
approaches are not the right approach.

00:04:58.100 --> 00:04:58.900 position:63%
For these problems,

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:01.000 position:63%
I mean, I think you'll get a lot more.

00:05:01.399 --> 00:05:03.170 position:63%
Why the jump to interplay between

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:05.149 position:63%
humans collaborating with these tools?

00:05:05.299 --> 00:05:07.352 position:63%
I can see one of these problems

00:05:07.352 --> 00:05:09.790 position:63%
being solved by smart humans assisted

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:12.099 position:63%
by some extremely powerful AI tools,

00:05:12.249 --> 00:05:14.106 position:63%
but the exact dynamic may be very

00:05:14.106 --> 00:05:16.399 position:63%
different from what we envision right now.

00:05:16.499 --> 00:05:18.567 position:63%
I mean, it could be a collaboration

00:05:18.567 --> 00:05:20.749 position:63%
of a type that just doesn't exist yet.

00:05:20.749 --> 00:05:22.596 position:63%
So I guess there's a couple of things that

00:05:22.596 --> 00:05:24.358 position:63%
could mean you could imagine like the AI

00:05:24.358 --> 00:05:26.076 position:63%
produces a leading proof of the Riemann

00:05:26.076 --> 00:05:26.576 position:63%
hypothesis.

00:05:26.891 --> 00:05:28.855 position:63%
this and uh it is not accompanied by an

00:05:28.855 --> 00:05:30.967 position:63%
exposition that that's one thing that that

00:05:30.967 --> 00:05:33.324 position:63%
could be the other thing it could actually mean

00:05:33.324 --> 00:05:35.485 position:63%
is maybe it is accompanied by an exposition

00:05:35.485 --> 00:05:37.744 position:63%
and that exposition is so complicated that no

00:05:37.744 --> 00:05:39.905 position:63%
human can grok it and that could even be an

00:05:39.905 --> 00:05:42.263 position:63%
intrinsic property of the exposition like maybe

00:05:42.263 --> 00:05:44.473 position:63%
it's so long that reading it would more than

00:05:44.473 --> 00:05:46.781 position:63%
a human lifetime so would that have value like

00:05:46.781 --> 00:05:49.138 position:63%
a little bit um not very much though right like

00:05:49.138 --> 00:05:51.103 position:63%
i'm already quite confident the Riemann

00:05:51.103 --> 00:05:52.177 position:63%
hypothesis is This is true.

00:05:52.627 --> 00:05:56.187 position:63%
Raising that confidence from, you know, 99% or 99.

00:05:56.187 --> 00:05:59.177 position:63%
9% to 100% is a little bit of information.

00:05:59.327 --> 00:06:01.377 position:63%
Would it like change my life as a mathematician?

00:06:01.477 --> 00:06:02.327 position:63%
Not super much.

00:06:03.027 --> 00:06:04.903 position:63%
On the other hand, if you're in this weaker

00:06:04.903 --> 00:06:06.949 position:63%
situation where the AI produces like lean proof

00:06:06.949 --> 00:06:08.910 position:63%
that's like poorly exposited or not exposited

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:10.658 position:63%
like but not intrinsically impossible to

00:06:10.658 --> 00:06:12.277 position:63%
understand, that would be a huge deal, right?

00:06:12.327 --> 00:06:13.877 position:63%
Like everyone would drop everything,

00:06:14.027 --> 00:06:15.747 position:63%
maybe not everyone, many mathematicians would

00:06:15.747 --> 00:06:16.727 position:63%
drop everything and like.

00:06:16.727 --> 00:06:19.407 position:63%
and we so do everything we could to translate it

00:06:19.407 --> 00:06:21.940 position:63%
into something human-readable. And I I see,

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:24.818 position:63%
again I see no reason why an AI that's superhuman

00:06:24.818 --> 00:06:27.523 position:63%
at math research wouldn't be able to help with

00:06:27.523 --> 00:06:30.285 position:63%
that expository task. You know I think the more

00:06:30.285 --> 00:06:32.933 position:63%
realistic situation is that the AI produces a

00:06:32.933 --> 00:06:35.696 position:63%
poorly exposited proof that's verified and lean

00:06:35.696 --> 00:06:38.401 position:63%
and then people and or the AI work together to

00:06:38.401 --> 00:06:39.437 position:63%
exposit it better.

00:06:39.687 --> 00:06:40.859 position:63%
We have a notion that it's

00:06:40.859 --> 00:06:41.987 position:63%
useful to prove something.

00:06:42.251 --> 00:06:44.518 position:63%
an interesting to prove something we have a

00:06:44.518 --> 00:06:46.992 position:63%
notion that it's useful to understand something

00:06:46.992 --> 00:06:49.568 position:63%
and typically in the history of mathematics those

00:06:49.568 --> 00:06:52.042 position:63%
two things have gone together and now we're the

00:06:52.042 --> 00:06:54.000 position:63%
state where they may come separately,

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.473 position:63%
where we may receive scrolls of ancient wisdom,

00:06:56.473 --> 00:06:58.329 position:63%
that we may receive like, you know,

00:06:58.329 --> 00:07:00.750 position:63%
notes from the Gods telling us that things are

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:03.172 position:63%
true without really being very clear at all on

00:07:03.172 --> 00:07:05.749 position:63%
why they're true. My hope is that that is in fact

00:07:05.749 --> 00:07:07.501 position:63%
not the way that it will work out.

00:07:07.947 --> 00:07:10.592 position:63%
That given these artefacts, perhaps,

00:07:10.592 --> 00:07:13.737 position:63%
this billion line lean proof that certifies

00:07:13.737 --> 00:07:16.597 position:63%
that the Riemann hypothesis is true, the

00:07:16.597 --> 00:07:17.047 position:63%
logarithmic Yeah.

00:07:17.047 --> 00:07:19.384 position:63%
models will also, as well as being superhuman

00:07:19.384 --> 00:07:21.669 position:63%
at producing proofs, will also be superhuman

00:07:21.669 --> 00:07:24.107 position:63%
at interpreting proofs and trying to understand

00:07:24.107 --> 00:07:26.241 position:63%
proofs. I think this is maybe the biggest

00:07:26.241 --> 00:07:28.730 position:63%
divergence I noticed yesterday at the conference

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:31.218 position:63%
between me and the other speakers. These things,

00:07:31.218 --> 00:07:33.047 position:63%
as well as being superhuman provers,

00:07:33.131 --> 00:07:35.231 position:63%
will also be superhuman explainers.

00:07:35.381 --> 00:07:37.306 position:63%
They're already excellent

00:07:37.306 --> 00:07:39.231 position:63%
at explaining known facts.

00:07:39.331 --> 00:07:41.523 position:63%
I'm a professional physicist and there

00:07:41.523 --> 00:07:44.277 position:63%
are things that I sort of should know but don't.

00:07:44.277 --> 00:07:46.189 position:63%
I go and in a way that I might be

00:07:46.189 --> 00:07:47.931 position:63%
embarrassed to ask a colleague,

00:07:48.081 --> 00:07:50.759 position:63%
I can ask these large language models and they

00:07:50.759 --> 00:07:53.267 position:63%
very non-judgmentally and patiently explain

00:07:53.267 --> 00:07:55.832 position:63%
all of these things that I should know to me

00:07:55.832 --> 00:07:58.681 position:63%
and now I do know them and I find them superhuman.

00:07:58.681 --> 00:08:00.349 position:63%
human at that. I find that they're

00:08:00.349 --> 00:08:02.367 position:63%
pretty much as good as any human would be,

00:08:02.417 --> 00:08:02.967 position:63%
perhaps,

00:08:03.017 --> 00:08:05.367 position:63%
you know, only as good as the very best humans,

00:08:05.417 --> 00:08:07.273 position:63%
but in any given domain they can

00:08:07.273 --> 00:08:09.017 position:63%
converse intelligently on that.

00:08:09.467 --> 00:08:11.695 position:63%
If that strength extends from being able

00:08:11.695 --> 00:08:13.597 position:63%
to explain things that are already

00:08:13.597 --> 00:08:15.771 position:63%
explained in textbooks to being able to

00:08:15.771 --> 00:08:18.217 position:63%
explain new things, and I imagine they would,

00:08:18.367 --> 00:08:21.150 position:63%
I think these models are going to be able

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:23.667 position:63%
to take these super complicated proofs

00:08:23.667 --> 00:08:24.818 position:63%
and try and break it down and

00:08:24.818 --> 00:08:26.248 position:63%
explain it and I think this is

00:08:26.248 --> 00:08:28.185 position:63%
something that models will be very good at

00:08:28.185 --> 00:08:30.807 position:63%
So if an AI system spits out, you know,

00:08:30.807 --> 00:08:33.232 position:63%
a million token proof of the Riemann

00:08:33.232 --> 00:08:36.235 position:63%
hypothesis and says, I got it, I don't go, yay,

00:08:36.335 --> 00:08:37.285 position:63%
okay, let's move on.

00:08:37.385 --> 00:08:38.635 position:63%
I go, what's the answer?

00:08:38.735 --> 00:08:39.485 position:63%
How do you do it?

00:08:40.385 --> 00:08:41.935 position:63%
Tell me. I have to understand.

00:08:42.035 --> 00:08:43.085 position:63%
That's why I'm doing this.

00:08:43.135 --> 00:08:44.073 position:63%
I'm not doing this for any

00:08:44.073 --> 00:08:45.185 position:63%
reason other than understanding.

00:08:45.771 --> 00:08:47.521 position:63%
If another mathematician comes up to me and says,

00:08:47.571 --> 00:08:48.771 position:63%
hey, I figured out the Riemann hypothesis.

00:08:48.921 --> 00:08:50.521 position:63%
I don't go, great, congratulations.

00:08:51.171 --> 00:08:53.164 position:63%
I go, what is it? I also go, great,

00:08:53.164 --> 00:08:55.021 position:63%
congratulations, but tell me the answer.

00:08:55.171 --> 00:08:56.271 position:63%
I want to understand.

00:08:56.521 --> 00:08:57.771 position:63%
Oh, it would be a huge value,

00:08:57.871 --> 00:08:59.471 position:63%
but it certainly wouldn't be a win.

00:09:00.299 --> 00:09:02.153 position:63%
It would be a massive amount of value

00:09:02.153 --> 00:09:04.106 position:63%
because there's probably some other LLM

00:09:04.106 --> 00:09:06.058 position:63%
that will take that god awful proof and

00:09:06.058 --> 00:09:08.449 position:63%
synthesize it and tell me what's really going on.

00:09:08.549 --> 00:09:11.078 position:63%
The reason proof is the mechanism by

00:09:11.078 --> 00:09:12.923 position:63%
which is our epistemology,

00:09:12.923 --> 00:09:15.999 position:63%
is the mechanism by which we arrive at truth,

00:09:16.149 --> 00:09:18.759 position:63%
is because we've been burned

00:09:18.759 --> 00:09:21.549 position:63%
so long on intuitive arguments.

00:09:22.731 --> 00:09:25.877 position:63%
And you probably know a thousand different,

00:09:25.877 --> 00:09:28.236 position:63%
you know, fake proofs of 1=0 and

00:09:28.236 --> 00:09:30.381 position:63%
mistakes in Euclid's Elements.

00:09:30.631 --> 00:09:32.881 position:63%
Human intuition is incredible

00:09:32.881 --> 00:09:34.831 position:63%
and it's also very faulty.

00:09:35.431 --> 00:09:37.724 position:63%
And for that reason, we've decided that we

00:09:37.724 --> 00:09:40.283 position:63%
need to have rigorous proof within an axiomatic

00:09:40.283 --> 00:09:42.362 position:63%
system as a mechanism for checking our

00:09:42.362 --> 00:09:44.708 position:63%
understanding. But that's not understanding

00:09:44.708 --> 00:09:45.208 position:63%
itself.

00:09:45.231 --> 00:09:47.581 position:63%
You know, you can understand a proof in a picture.

00:09:48.683 --> 00:09:51.688 position:63%
You can say, I see very clearly what's going on.

00:09:51.688 --> 00:09:54.055 position:63%
Yes, I have the technique to convert what I

00:09:54.055 --> 00:09:56.233 position:63%
see clearly into an argument in language,

00:09:56.383 --> 00:09:58.233 position:63%
and that's like the gold standard.

00:09:58.735 --> 00:10:00.535 position:63%
But the understanding happens somewhere else.

00:10:00.535 --> 00:10:03.841 position:63%
On the one hand, I am kind of excited

00:10:03.841 --> 00:10:07.235 position:63%
to see what these models can really do.

00:10:07.335 --> 00:10:08.335 position:63%
And I think I'm certainly,

00:10:08.435 --> 00:10:10.385 position:63%
I'm kind of cheering on them.

00:10:10.485 --> 00:10:12.308 position:63%
I'm really hoping that at some point

00:10:12.308 --> 00:10:14.335 position:63%
DeepMind just comes out and says, hey,

00:10:14.385 --> 00:10:16.435 position:63%
our model proved the Riemann hypothesis.

00:10:16.685 --> 00:10:18.035 position:63%
Here's the lean proof.

00:10:18.235 --> 00:10:21.135 position:63%
I'm confronted also with this kind of skepticism

00:10:21.135 --> 00:10:24.035 position:63%
like, oh, will these models really make progress?

00:10:24.387 --> 00:10:26.587 position:63%
And I'm actually always on the side with,

00:10:26.687 --> 00:10:28.857 position:63%
I mean, I think you should wait and see

00:10:28.857 --> 00:10:31.137 position:63%
or you should give them a few more months.

00:10:31.187 --> 00:10:34.307 position:63%
On the other hand, I am somewhat

00:10:34.307 --> 00:10:37.333 position:63%
concerned about kind of if this

00:10:37.333 --> 00:10:40.737 position:63%
progress is actually extremely fast.

00:10:41.443 --> 00:10:43.043 position:63%
Then there's all these questions,

00:10:43.093 --> 00:10:46.363 position:63%
will these models really continue to act in our

00:10:46.363 --> 00:10:49.702 position:63%
best interest or will they kind of start to veer

00:10:49.702 --> 00:10:51.883 position:63%
off, do some misaligned things?

00:10:51.883 --> 00:10:54.949 position:63%
Because we already see that many of the most

00:10:54.949 --> 00:10:57.471 position:63%
capable models like O3, for example,

00:10:57.471 --> 00:10:59.243 position:63%
was a very notorious liar.

00:10:59.743 --> 00:11:01.883 position:63%
Historically, when something becomes

00:11:01.883 --> 00:11:03.793 position:63%
cheap or commoditized in society,

00:11:04.143 --> 00:11:06.302 position:63%
the things we value become orthogonalized

00:11:06.302 --> 00:11:07.793 position:63%
with respect to those direct.

00:11:07.793 --> 00:11:08.293 position:63%
directions.

00:11:08.465 --> 00:11:10.053 position:63%
I think it's very true and it's a good

00:11:10.053 --> 00:11:11.316 position:63%
lens to think about, you know,

00:11:11.316 --> 00:11:12.946 position:63%
the changes that are going to happen to

00:11:12.946 --> 00:11:14.657 position:63%
the math and theoretical computer science

00:11:14.657 --> 00:11:15.157 position:63%
community.

00:11:15.615 --> 00:11:17.225 position:63%
But the question is what is

00:11:17.225 --> 00:11:19.065 position:63%
going to be commoditized, right?

00:11:19.165 --> 00:11:20.826 position:63%
What is going to become cheap

00:11:20.826 --> 00:11:22.765 position:63%
and less valued than it was before?

00:11:23.265 --> 00:11:25.609 position:63%
And what are the orthogonal directions

00:11:25.609 --> 00:11:28.015 position:63%
that are going to survive for it, right?

00:11:28.315 --> 00:11:30.111 position:63%
And it does seem to me that

00:11:30.111 --> 00:11:32.165 position:63%
certain types of problem solving

00:11:32.451 --> 00:11:35.251 position:63%
are going to become cheaper.

00:11:36.291 --> 00:11:39.123 position:63%
Uh we're gonna value a little bit less over time.

00:11:39.123 --> 00:11:41.900 position:63%
Now there can still be very challenging problems

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:44.506 position:63%
that, you know, when you solve them, Riemann,

00:11:44.506 --> 00:11:47.282 position:63%
you know, boy, what an amazing set of tools that

00:11:47.282 --> 00:11:49.662 position:63%
would be to solve such a question, right?

00:11:49.662 --> 00:11:52.268 position:63%
So maybe these amazing landmark problems will

00:11:52.268 --> 00:11:53.967 position:63%
all still survive, who knows?

00:11:53.967 --> 00:11:55.441 position:63%
Could be wrong about that.

00:11:55.541 --> 00:11:57.774 position:63%
Move 37 was a move made by AlphaGo,

00:11:57.774 --> 00:12:00.070 position:63%
i in one of the games to beat one of

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:02.491 position:63%
the best human Go players in the world.

00:12:02.491 --> 00:12:03.039 position:63%
world and

00:12:03.811 --> 00:12:06.395 position:63%
When someone asks, is this a move 37 for X_

00:12:06.395 --> 00:12:09.273 position:63%
or is this a move 37 for whatever uh discipline,

00:12:09.273 --> 00:12:11.798 position:63%
one is maybe kind of at a conceptual level

00:12:11.798 --> 00:12:14.324 position:63%
asking, you know, is this the moment where

00:12:14.324 --> 00:12:16.967 position:63%
the machine uh overtakes the best human in a

00:12:16.967 --> 00:12:19.375 position:63%
particular domain. So I would say that's

00:12:19.375 --> 00:12:22.018 position:63%
resoundingly no. Um so I would say that such

00:12:22.018 --> 00:12:24.602 position:63%
a move 37 moment might come when uh machine

00:12:24.602 --> 00:12:27.245 position:63%
produces the proof of the remount of process

00:12:27.245 --> 00:12:29.829 position:63%
or millennium problem or even comes up with

00:12:29.829 --> 00:12:30.711 position:63%
a a deep theory

00:12:30.711 --> 00:12:32.696 position:63%
a theory that really synthesizes all these

00:12:32.696 --> 00:12:34.509 position:63%
different fields in one fell swoop.

00:12:34.509 --> 00:12:36.725 position:63%
I would consider that to be maybe a move 37

00:12:36.725 --> 00:12:37.531 position:63%
for mathematics.

00:12:37.581 --> 00:12:40.229 position:63%
Every time that a theorem or open

00:12:40.229 --> 00:12:43.578 position:63%
problem is solved, to be good mathematics,

00:12:43.578 --> 00:12:45.681 position:63%
the solution isn't the end.

00:12:45.731 --> 00:12:46.231 position:63%
Mm-hmm.

00:12:46.381 --> 00:12:48.436 position:63%
Someone solves the Riemann hypothesis,

00:12:48.436 --> 00:12:50.596 position:63%
maybe that's the end of a lot of things,

00:12:50.596 --> 00:12:52.757 position:63%
but I can't think of many problems where

00:12:52.757 --> 00:12:55.181 position:63%
the solution by itself genuinely marks an end.

00:12:56.323 --> 00:13:01.823 position:63%
And so I think you'll discover that what we learn

00:13:01.823 --> 00:13:06.883 position:63%
from solved problems will be used to generate

00:13:06.883 --> 00:13:12.273 position:63%
new problems and new conjectures and the pursuit

00:13:12.273 --> 00:13:17.773 position:63%
of knowledge about integers and primes will go on.

